WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.000
A doorway, a line at two metres.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.780
A crowd walks through.

3
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.040
Every head passes under it.

4
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.100
The model: adult heights
in a town are normal,

5
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.490
mean one hundred and seventy centimetres,

6
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.260
standard deviation seven point five.

7
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.170
So how rare is a two-metre adult?

8
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.300
One in forty?

9
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.000
One in seven hundred?

10
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.690
In this mission, you'll
meet the normal curve:

11
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.280
bell-shaped, symmetric about the mean.

12
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.000
You'll use the rule: about sixty-eight,
ninety-five and ninety-nine point seven

13
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:36.180
per cent of values lie within one, two
and three standard deviations of the mean.

14
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.500
And you'll find probabilities
as areas under the curve,

15
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.130
on your GDC.

16
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: find how rare a
two-metre adult is under this model.
